{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Config-driven status mapping (map-or-drift, collapse round-trip via rebar-status labels)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStatus mapping is hardcoded across Jira-family paths: outbound reads the built-in\n`value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` at **four** consumer sites (Scope), mirrored a fifth time as\n`config.local_to_jira_status`; inbound inverts `config.jira_to_local_status` and prefers the\n`rebar-status:<local>` label, whose stamping is hardcoded to `blocked`/`cancelled`\n(`outbound_labels._STATUS_ANNOTATION_LABEL`). A project lacking a rebar status has no\necho-safe remap; a config collapse over others has no label to stamp/recover. Status must become config-driven on\nthe S1 core: always **map-or-drift** (never skip a ticket); any non-injective collapse must\nround-trip via `rebar-status:`.\n\n## Dependency (prerequisite ticket)\n\nWires the status axis onto the S1 mapping core **[rebar:bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141]** (on `main`).\n`rebar_reconciler.mapping_config` provides `load_mapping_config(root=None)` and\n`resolve_for_project(config, project_key, *, builtin) -> MappingLayer` (merges\n`builtin ← [mapping.default] ← [mapping.projects.<KEY>]`) with `MappingLayer.status_map`\n(resolved local→Jira; `SKIP` = intentional drop; a status ABSENT is the drift case).\n`LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` is the `builtin`, so with no `[mapping]` config the effective map equals\ntoday's default — existing behaviour and parity tests unchanged.\n\n## Approach — one resolution seam, threaded through existing consumers\n\n1. **`config.py` — resolution entry point.** Add `effective_status_map(project_key, root=None)`\n   and `effective_jira_to_local(project_key, root=None)`, each calling\n   `load_mapping_config` + `resolve_for_project` with `builtin=LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`\n   (forward) / the canonical `jira_to_local_status` (reverse = canonical preimage plus\n   config's reverse overrides, NOT a naive inversion). The literal dicts stay the built-in\n   fallback (in lock-step with `value_maps` by the parity test).\n   `mapping_config` is imported LAZILY inside the function (config.py stays stdlib-only at\n   top level).\n\n2. **Outbound consumers read the resolved map.** The project key is resolved once per ticket\n   in `outbound_differ` (where `projects_store.resolve_project(ticket, mapping)` already runs)\n   and threaded to the mappers as optional `status_map: dict|None`; `None` → built-in fallback\n   (untouched paths unchanged). Sites: `outbound_mapper.map_fields_to_remote` (shared UPDATE,\n   Cloud+DC), `jira/outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` (Cloud CREATE),\n   `jira_datacenter/backend` create, `jira/acli` transition name.\n\n3. **Drift = leave Jira as-is, never a per-mutation failure.** Drift is decided ONLY in the\n   mapper (which holds the effective map): with no entry for a local status the mapper **omits\n   the `status` field** (rebar keeps its status; Jira unchanged) and records a drift alert —\n   replacing today's `.get(status,\"To Do\")` coerce. `reconcile_helpers.preflight_status_mapping`\n   needs NO change: it runs pass-wide AFTER the differ/mapper (`reconcile.py:485`), so a drifted\n   mutation already carries no `status` field and preflight's existing skip-when-no-status\n   branch makes it non-offending; mapped mutations carry the Jira NAME, which preflight already\n   tolerates. Kill-switch untouched.\n\n4. **Generalised `rebar-status:` round-trip.** Replace the hardcoded blocked/cancelled maps\n   with derivation from the effective map. Outbound (`outbound_labels`): stamp\n   `rebar-status:<local>` **iff `effective_jira_to_local[status_map[local]] != local`** — each\n   collapse group's canonical-preimage member (named by the reverse map) stays UNANNOTATED,\n   every other member is annotated. On the built-in map this observably selects exactly\n   {blocked, cancelled}: in_progress/closed are the canonical preimages; the third \"Done\"\n   member `deleted` never reaches stamping (pre-existing `outbound_differ`\n   `excluded_statuses={archived,deleted}` skip) — so default stamping is bit-for-bit preserved.\n   Inbound (parse-helper sites below): recover by **parsing the\n   `rebar-status:<local>` suffix** against the effective reverse vocabulary, via one shared\n   helper so the sites can't drift. Label-first precedence unchanged. A DRIFTED status (absent\n   from `status_map`) has no Jira target → no label stamped. A malformed `[mapping]` fails\n   closed: `load_mapping_config` raises S1's `MappingConfigError` at the resolution seam.\n\n5. **Parity preserved.** `value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` / `config.local_to_jira_status`\n   stay the built-in literal (the injected `builtin`), so existing parity tests stay green.\n\n## Scope (files)\n\n- `config.py` — `effective_status_map`/`effective_jira_to_local` (lazy `mapping_config`).\n- `outbound_differ.py` — resolve project key once; thread effective `status_map` to mappers + label diff.\n- `adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py` — optional `status_map`; drift-omit on unmapped; built-in fallback.\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` — Cloud CREATE reads effective map, built-in fallback.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` — DC CREATE reads effective map, built-in fallback.\n- `adapters/jira/acli.py` — transition name via effective map.\n- `outbound_labels.py` — canonical-preimage stamp rule from the effective map.\n- `inbound_fields.py` — label-first recovery by parsing `rebar-status:<local>` (shared helper).\n- `inbound_translate.py` / `apply_inbound_events.py` / `inbound_differ.py` — use the shared parse helper (retire the duplicated `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL`).\n- `applier.py` — re-export the shared helper in `__all__` (replaces the retired literal).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py` (new) — behavioral oracle.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **in-process unit** — translation is pure over the resolved map; oracle = produced/\nomitted field, stamped label, recovered status, drift alert. Tests hit the REAL entry points\n(`config.effective_status_map`, the outbound mappers,\n`outbound_labels._diff_status_annotation_labels`, `inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields`),\nnever copies.\n\n- **Config-effect contrast:** `default.status_map` `blocked→\"To Do\"` → outbound targets `To\n  Do`; no override → built-in default. `test_status_config_effect`.\n- **Drift:** unmapped status → mapper omits `status` (asserted on the mutation lacking\n  `status` + captured stderr), not a crash, not a coerced `To Do`. `test_unmapped_status_drifts`.\n- **Collapse round-trip:** a config collapse over a NON blocked/cancelled pair stamps each\n  `rebar-status:<local>`; inbound recovers each by parsing the label — both directions.\n  `test_status_collapse_roundtrip`.\n- **Parity:** existing `value_maps`↔`config` parity tests stay green.\n\n**Drift alert provenance:** a non-fatal stderr line from the mapper (no new subsystem); oracle\nasserts on captured stderr (`capsys`) + the omitted field. **Rollback:** config-gated — no\n`[mapping]` section ⇒ effective map = built-in default (maps every status), the drift branch is\nunreachable, today's behaviour preserved; label FORMAT unchanged, back-out is a plain revert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Effective map = `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` ← `[mapping.default]` ← `[mapping.projects.<KEY>]`\n  via S1 `resolve_for_project`; a non-default overlay changes the outbound target through the\n  real mapper path — `test_status_mapping.py::test_status_config_effect`.\n- [ ] An unmapped status **drifts**: the outbound mutation omits the `status` field (Jira\n  unchanged) and a non-fatal drift warning is recorded; the ticket is never skipped nor\n  recorded as a per-mutation failure — verified by\n  `test_status_mapping.py::test_unmapped_status_drifts`.\n- [ ] A config-collapsed pair (statuses OTHER than blocked/cancelled) round-trips losslessly\n  via `rebar-status:<local>` labels — `test_status_mapping.py::test_status_collapse_roundtrip`.\n- [ ] The `value_maps`↔`config` parity tests in `state/test_config.py` remain green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787333573557257001,"uuid":"f5d0dfe5-ada8-4c9f-82b2-695edcd1e9ec"}